pus-driven findings drove the result: the cost controls fix the multipliers at cap_bounding_add \u00d74 and seccomp_rule_add \u00d71 (both consistent pairs were settled and the cheaper shrunk plan kept), and 94 atoms are forbidden because, applied alone, each admits a must_deny run \u2014 those are excluded from the plan however cheap they are. The plan holds 246 atoms across 8 rounds; it admits 142 of the 146 must_admit runs, the remaining 4 are recorded as residuals with status nonconvergent (the cap of eight rounds was reached while they were still denied), and all 84 must_deny runs stay refused under the plan. Every one of the 246 atoms carries a witness run, the layer and the sequence at which the plan without it refuses that run. Determinism was proved two ways: a repeat run is byte-identical, and a corpus with every record re-listed in a different order produces byte-identical artifacts.\n\nThe closing figures, each worked out across the rows:\n\n- Total events the five repair rules corrected between them (an event corrected by two rules counts once for each): **2211** \u2014 arch 590, capability 370, number 588, perm 68, type 595.\n- Permissible atoms that repair no run that must be admitted: **1033** (1106 permissible atoms in the catalogue, of which 73 repair at least one must_admit run).\n- Mean cost of the atoms in the plan, rounded half-even to two decimal places: **3.38** (total effective cost 831 over 246 atoms).\n- Principals whose final disposition is granted: **84**."}`; `0b27b9dc-7985-54f1-a120-46e6810315a3/trajectories/glm-5.3/run_1/trajectory_usage.json:$[0].model_name` = `"glm-5.3"`; `0b27b9dc-7985-54f1-a120-46e6810315a3/trajectories/glm-5.3/run_1/trajectory_usage.json:$[0].trajectory_input_tokens` = `27239570`; `0b27b9dc-7985-54f1-a120-46e6810315a3/trajectories/glm-5.3/run_1/trajectory_usage.json:$[0].trajectory_input_cache_tokens` = `26979275`; `0b27b9dc-7985-54f1-a120-46e6810315a3/trajectories/glm-5.3/run_1/trajectory_usage.json:$[0].traject