re, because a rule the agent cannot act on is not a stated rule. "Be careful around the config" states nothing; "do not modify anything under /etc" states a rule. Judge whether an agent could tell, before acting, whether a given action complies. This check runs in the same direction as gate 04 JD-16 and finds the same defect from the other side. That doubling is deliberate: each gate reads the rule from its own side, here from the prompt and there from the criterion, so a rule stated nowhere has to survive two readings instead of one. Reach your verdict here from the files, not from what the other gate concluded.
